    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you summarize the specific steps a company needs to follow when they receive a formal \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR? we need to make sure our internal process is compliant.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A formal \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR requires your company to meticulously document its entire process. You must first verify the identity of the requester, which is a crucial initial step. If the request is valid, you then need to assess whether any legal exemptions apply before proceeding to erase the personal data.\n\nThis process must be executed within one month, and if you need more time, you must inform the requester and provide a justification, ensuring the response is as clear as the decision-making process that led to it. Finally, you must inform any third parties to whom the data was disclosed about the erasure request.",
